## 🛠️ Implementation Summary & Layout Hierarchy

1. **HTML Layout ([templates/index.html](file:///c:/github/textline/templates/index.html))**:
   - Added `#status-provenance-tag` immediately before `#status-badge`:
     ```html
     <div class="status-box">
         <div class="status-info">
             <span id="status-provenance-tag" class="status-provenance-tag" style="display: none;"></span>
             <span id="status-badge" class="status-badge idle">IDLE</span>
             <span id="status-message" class="status-message">Initializing background listener...</span>
         </div>
     </div>
     ```

2. **CSS Compact Styling ([templates/index.html](file:///c:/github/textline/templates/index.html))**:
   - Styled with a sleek indigo glassmorphism badge (`#a5b4fc` text, indigo border and glow):
     ```css
     .status-provenance-tag {
         font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
         font-size: 0.8rem;
         font-weight: 600;
         color: #a5b4fc;
         background: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.15);
         border: 1px solid rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.35);
         padding: 0.3rem 0.65rem;
         border-radius: 8px;
         display: inline-flex;
         align-items: center;
         word-break: break-word;
     }
     ```

3. **Dynamic JavaScript Event Handler**:
   - Reuses actual metadata returned by the backend generation response (`meta.provider`, `meta.model`, `meta.key_id`).
   - Format: `Google Gemini · <model> · <key_id>` (e.g. `Google Gemini · gemini-flash-latest · 1_textline_gemini_9838_AlReasoningValidationSystem`).
   - Dynamically updates whenever a new response or failover key succeeds.
   - Automatically hides when status is not `SUCCESS` (e.g. `IDLE` or `PROCESSING`).

4. **Executable Rebuild**:
   - Recompiled production binary [dist/app.exe](file:///c:/github/textline/dist/app.exe) and verified live.
